# 🔐 1. Access Control Decorator

A decorator can check a condition before allowing a function to execute.

## Basic Logic

```text
Function Call
     ↓
Decorator
     ↓
Check Condition
   ↙       ↘
 True      False
  ↓          ↓
Run        Access
Function   Denied
```

### Example

```python
def access_control(function):
    def wrapper():
        logged_in = True

        if logged_in:
            function()
        else:
            print("Access Denied")

    return wrapper


@access_control
def profile():
    print("Welcome to your profile")


profile()
```

